00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.070 align:start position:0%
eu finance ministers have approved an  updated mandate to finalize negotiations  with the european parliament on the  establishment of a single resolution  mechanism for banks  the council wants the talks to be  concluded in time for the plenary  session in april before the end of the  current parliamentary term  these discussions in council on all  these issues  were extensive  difficult  but constructive  and we have arrived at the new updated  mandate of the council to the presidency  which allows us  the necessary flexibility to go to trial  tomorrow with the parliament the single  resolution mechanism is one of the key  elements of the banking union it aims to  enable in-depth restructuring of banks  in serious financial problems  the council also discussed tougher rules  on the taxation of savings income the  idea is to enable member states to  better clamp down on tax fraud and tax  evasion  the presidency hopes the new rules will  be adopted before the end of march  following endorsement by eu leaders  ministers have also exchanged views on  the economic elements of the eu 2030  energy and climate framework
 

